pañcavidyāsthānāni|{rig pa'i gnas lnga'i ming la} (Skt. pañcavidyāsthānāni) names of the five major fields of study
śabdavidyā|{sgra'i rig pa} (Skt. śabdavidyā) science of sound or Sanskrit
sarvāśravakṣayajñānavaiśāradyam|{zag pa zad pa thams cad mkhyen pa la mi 'jigs pa} (Skt. sarvāśrava-kṣaya-jñāna-vaiśāradyam) intrepidity in knowing that that all imperfections have come to an end
hetuvidyā|{gtan tshigs kyi rig pa} (Skt. hetuvidyā) logic or philosophy
adhyātmavidyā|{nang gi rig pa} (Skt. adhyātmavidyā) the doctrine of inner science
cikitsāvidyā|{gso ba'i rig pa} (Skt. cikitsāvidyā) healing science
catvāri dharmasamādānāni|{chos yang dag par len pa bzhi'i ming la} (Skt. catvāri dharmasamādānāni) four pure moral maxims
pratyutpannasukham āyatyāṃ duḥkhavipākaṃ|{da ltar byung ba la bde la phyi ma la rnam par smin pa sdug bsngal ba} (Skt. pratyutpannasukham āyatyāṃ duḥkhavipākaṃ) the happiness of the present life will turn into suffering in the next life
pratyutpannaduḥkham āyatyāṃ sukhavipākam|{da ltar byung ba la sdug bsngal la phyi ma la rnam par smin pa bde ba} (Skt. pratyutpannaduḥkham āyatyāṃ sukhavipākam) the fruit of the sufferings in this life will be happiness in the next life
pratyutpannaduḥkham āyatyāṃ duḥkhavipākam|{da ltar byung ba la yang sdug bsngal ba la phyi ma la rnam par smin pa sdug bsngal ba} (Skt. pratyutpannaduḥkham āyatyāṃ duḥkhavipākam) happiness in this life will bring forth fruits of happiness in the next world also
pratyutpannasuḥkham āyatyāṃ sukhavipākam|{da ltar byung ba la yang bde ba la phyi ma la rnam par smin pa bde ba} (Skt. pratyutpannasuḥkham āyatyāṃ sukhavipākam) misery in this life will produce misery in the next world also
